==============================================================================================================
(b) P-representation (Gaussian, random phases) -> kinetic sum over unordered graviton pairs
==============================================================================================================
  diagonal m_ii zero: <|A|^2>_P = 35.78679 +- 0.02932;  sum_(i<j) N_i N_j |m_ij|^2 (+ (1/2) sum N_i^2 |m_ii|^2) = 35.81472
  diagonal m_ii kept: <|A|^2>_P = 45.97412 +- 0.03884;  sum_(i<j) N_i N_j |m_ij|^2 (+ (1/2) sum N_i^2 |m_ii|^2) = 45.97635
  a single COHERENT state with the same N_i (|A|^2 / incoherent value):
     all phases equal      : 2.6017
     fixed random phases #0: 0.7950
     fixed random phases #1: 0.0459
     fixed random phases #2: 0.5693
  => the incoherent rate is the phase average of the coherent one; interference between different graviton
     pairs feeding the same final state is what a coherent state adds (it can raise or lower the rate).
  continuum: sum_{i<j} = (1/2) sum_{i != j}  ->  Gamma = (1/2) sum_{l1 l2} int dn_l1 dn_l2 sigma_{l1 l2} v_rel,
             v_rel = 1 - cos theta_12 (massless Moller flux); no zero-point (1/2) term: normal ordering.

==============================================================================================================
(c) isotropic gas: Gamma = (8 pi/15) G^2 rho^2 ?  (sympy, then module two-beam route)
==============================================================================================================
Gamma (physical helicities)            = 32*pi*G**2*n_m*n_p*omega**2/15  ; with n_p w = rho_p, n_m w = rho_m: 32*pi*G**2*rho_m*rho_p/15
unpolarised (rho_p = rho_m = rho/2)     = 8*pi*G**2*rho**2/15   ;  B&O eq. 14: 8 pi G^2 rho^2/15 ; ratio = 1
helicity fraction p of +2:  Gamma/(8 pi G^2 rho^2/15) = 4*p*(1 - p)  -> 0 for a fully circularly polarised background
if eq. 6's equal labels were PHYSICAL helicities (same-helicity pairs radiate):  Gamma/(8 pi G^2 rho^2/15) = 4*p**2 - 4*p + 2  (= 1 only at p = 1/2: eq. 14 is blind to the label reading)
spectrum: sigma v ~ k1 k2, so Gamma = (32 pi/15) G^2 (int k dn_+)(int k dn_-) = (8 pi/15) G^2 rho^2 for ANY isotropic unpolarised spectrum (the integrand factorises).

module route: beams_pair_rate (full amplitude, module phase space), Gauss-Legendre average over cos(theta_12)
  w1=1.0, w2=1.0: <sigma v>(R,L)/(w1 w2) = 6.702064327658 [sympy: 32 pi/15 = 6.702064327658],  (R,R)/(w1 w2) = 7.92e-30;  (1/2)<sigma v>_unpol/(w1 w2) = 1.675516081915  [8 pi/15 = 1.675516081915]
  w1=0.5, w2=2.0: <sigma v>(R,L)/(w1 w2) = 6.702064327658 [sympy: 32 pi/15 = 6.702064327658],  (R,R)/(w1 w2) = 3.13e-29;  (1/2)<sigma v>_unpol/(w1 w2) = 1.675516081915  [8 pi/15 = 1.675516081915]
  w1=0.3, w2=1.7: <sigma v>(R,L)/(w1 w2) = 6.702064327658 [sympy: 32 pi/15 = 6.702064327658],  (R,R)/(w1 w2) = 1.25e-28;  (1/2)<sigma v>_unpol/(w1 w2) = 1.675516081915  [8 pi/15 = 1.675516081915]
  two-line isotropic spectrum (60% at 0.3, 40% at 1.7, unpolarised, n = 1): Gamma/rho^2 = 1.675516081915  (8 pi/15 = 1.675516081915)

==============================================================================================================
(c') B&O's coherent/incoherent comparison: eq. 8 vs eq. 14 for N gravitons in a volume V
==============================================================================================================
eq.8 / (eq.14 x V) = 9*V*omega*sigma**2/(40*pi**2) ;  equal when V w sigma^2 = 40*pi**2/9  (B&O: 40 pi^2/9)
V_eff with sigma = eps w, w = 2 pi/lambda: 5*lambda**3/(9*pi*epsilon**2)  (B&O: 5 lambda^3/(9 pi eps^2));  eps = 0.1: 17.68 lambda^3; eps = 0.15: 7.86 lambda^3

==============================================================================================================
(d) number emissivity 2 dP/dtdV with Delta N_eff-allowed rho_GW (SI)
==============================================================================================================
units: Gamma_nat = (8 pi/15) G_nat^2 rho_nat^2 -> Gamma_SI = (8 pi/15) G^2 rho_E^2 / c^7 (pairs m^-3 s^-1);
       G_nat = G/(hbar c^5), rho_nat = rho_E (hbar c)^3, rate density / (hbar^4 c^3): hbar cancels.
rho_gamma(T0 = 2.7255 K) = 4.1748e-14 J/m^3 ; rho_crit(H0 = 67.4) = 7.6689e-10 J/m^3
Planck 2018 abstract: N_eff = 2.99 +- 0.17 (68%), SM 3.044 -> Delta N_eff <~ 0.3 at 2 sigma
  Delta N_eff = 0.10: rho_GW = 9.481e-16 J/m^3 (Omega_GW h^2 = 5.62e-07);  Gamma = 3.08e-110 pairs m^-3 s^-1;  2 Gamma = 6.17e-110 photons m^-3 s^-1
  Delta N_eff = 0.20: rho_GW = 1.896e-15 J/m^3 (Omega_GW h^2 = 1.12e-06);  Gamma = 1.23e-109 pairs m^-3 s^-1;  2 Gamma = 2.47e-109 photons m^-3 s^-1
  Delta N_eff = 0.29: rho_GW = 2.750e-15 J/m^3 (Omega_GW h^2 = 1.63e-06);  Gamma = 2.59e-109 pairs m^-3 s^-1;  2 Gamma = 5.19e-109 photons m^-3 s^-1
  Delta N_eff = 0.50: rho_GW = 4.741e-15 J/m^3 (Omega_GW h^2 = 2.81e-06);  Gamma = 7.71e-109 pairs m^-3 s^-1;  2 Gamma = 1.54e-108 photons m^-3 s^-1
  B&O's '2 dP/dtdV ~ 1e-110 m^-3 s^-1' needs rho_GW = 3.82e-16 J/m^3, i.e. Delta N_eff = 0.040 (Omega_GW h^2 = 2.3e-07)
  energy emissivity for photons of energy hbar*omega: 2 Gamma hbar omega (linear in hbar)
  with the CMB stimulated factor (1 + 2 f), nu = 1e-09 Hz: 1 + 2 f = 1.14e+20 -> 2 Gamma (1 + 2 f) = 5.9e-89 m^-3 s^-1 (monochromatic estimate)
  with the CMB stimulated factor (1 + 2 f), nu = 1e+02 Hz: 1 + 2 f = 1.14e+09 -> 2 Gamma (1 + 2 f) = 5.9e-100 m^-3 s^-1 (monochromatic estimate)

