(e) depletion: Gamma_1(k), B&O eqs. 15 / S9 and |Phi|
==============================================================================================================
Gamma_1(k1) per unit partner density at energy k2: 16*pi*G**2*k1*k2/15  -> int dn_2: (16 pi/15) G^2 k1 rho  (rho = int k2 dn_2)
check: int dn_1 Gamma_1 = (16 pi/15) G^2 rho^2 = 2 x Gamma(eq. 14) (two gravitons per pair): 2
module: Gamma_1/(k1 rho) for k1 = 0.8, partners at 1.9 = 3.351032163829; 16 pi/15 = 3.351032163829
d Y/dz from the physical collision rate (k_phys = (1+z) k0): 16*pi*G**2*k0*rho_co*(z + 1)**4*Y(z)/(15*H)
B&O S9 right side:                                          16*pi*G**2*k0*rho_co*(z + 1)**4*Y(z)/(15*H)  -> identical (k = comoving / today's momentum)

formal solution check (toy units G = 1, H(z) = (1+z)^2, y(k, z_i) = k e^{-k}, z from 3 to 0):
  max |y(k,0) exp(-k Phi(z_i)) - y(k,z_i)| / max y = 1.9e-05;  depletion of rho_co: 0.3322  (high-k end depleted most: y(k=20,0)/y(k=20,z_i) = 4.134e-07, y(k=1,0)/y(k=1,z_i) = 0.4795)

|Phi| in SI: exponent = omega0 * |Phi|, |Phi| = int_0^z (16 pi/15)(G^2 hbar/c^7)(1+z)^4 rho_co / H(z) dz  [s]
  Delta N_eff = 0.29, rho_co = 2.75e-15 J/m^3, z_max = 1e28 (T = 2.3e+15 GeV), constant Omega_r: |Phi| = 3.16e-25 s   (B&O: ~1e-25 Hz^-1)
