      nu0 = 1e+09 Hz: omega0|Phi| = 2.0e-15;  with CMB-stimulated (1 + 2f): 2.3e-13
  Delta N_eff = 0.29, rho_co = 2.75e-15 J/m^3, z_max = 1e28 (T = 2.3e+15 GeV), g_* steps: |Phi| = 5.09e-25 s   (B&O: ~1e-25 Hz^-1)
      nu0 = 1e-09 Hz: omega0|Phi| = 3.2e-33;  with CMB-stimulated (1 + 2f): 3.6e-13
      nu0 = 1e+02 Hz: omega0|Phi| = 3.2e-22;  with CMB-stimulated (1 + 2f): 3.6e-13
      nu0 = 1e+09 Hz: omega0|Phi| = 3.2e-15;  with CMB-stimulated (1 + 2f): 3.6e-13

caveat (plasma): relativistic e+- plasma, omega_pl = e T/3 = 0.101 T; GW today at nu0 << GHz has k/T = 1.8e-09 (100 Hz), so 2-photon final states (photon energies ~k) are below the plasma cutoff while the plasma is relativistic: S9 integrated to z ~ 1e28 overstates even this tiny depletion.
        today's mean (fully ionised) n_e = 0.22 m^-3 -> omega_pl0 = 26.5 rad/s; nHz PTA photons cannot propagate at all.
